{{!-- "By the numbers" — a hairline-ruled row of figures about the publication.

	{{> "about/stats"}}                     A1's, where the centred hero already provides the space
	{{> "about/stats" padding="pt-14"}}     A2's, under the ruled-off split hero

	padding   the section's top padding

EVERY FIGURE IS COUNTED, NOT WRITTEN. The design source hardcodes four numbers; a publication's
About page that says 104 posts a year after it said 104 posts is worse than no figure at all. Each
one is a `limit="1"` query read for its pagination total — asking for one row answers "how many
are there" without loading them — and the year is the oldest post's, so "publishing since" moves
when the archive does.

THE WRITER COUNT IS STAFF ACCOUNTS, NOT PUBLISHED WRITERS, the same as the Feed's masthead line:
`count.posts` is not filterable on authors in Ghost 6, and Handlebars cannot count the rows a
loop's own guard kept. On a publication with an unpublished staff account this figure reads one
higher than the masthead below it. Recorded as a concession in DECISIONS.md.

A FIGURE OF ZERO IS NOT A FIGURE. Every cell is guarded on its own total, so a publication with no
**Tags** loses the "Subjects" cell rather than announcing a 36px `0` on the page a buyer is most
likely to be looking at on their first day. That is ADR 0003, and the auto-fit grid below re-flows
the remaining cells without any help. "Publishing since" was already guarded — on `oldest` rather
than on a total, because its value is a date and not a count.

The 1px grid gap over a border-coloured background is what draws the dividers, so the cells sit on
`--surface` rather than carrying borders of their own — one rule instead of four, and no doubled
line where two cells meet. --}}
<section
	aria-label="{{t "By the numbers"}}"
	class="container {{#if padding}}{{padding}}{{/if}}">
	<dl
		class="border-border bg-border grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(160px,100%),1fr))] gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-md border">
		{{#get "posts" limit="1" as |rows posts|}}
			{{#if posts.total}}
				<div class="bg-surface px-6 py-[26px]">
					<dt class="text-muted font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Posts published"}}</dt>
					<dd class="font-display tracking-display mt-2.5 text-4xl font-medium">{{posts.total}}</dd>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}

		{{#get "authors" limit="1" as |rows writers|}}
			{{#if writers.total}}
				<div class="bg-surface px-6 py-[26px]">
					<dt class="text-muted font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Writers"}}</dt>
					<dd class="font-display tracking-display mt-2.5 text-4xl font-medium">{{writers.total}}</dd>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}

		{{#get "tags" limit="1" as |rows subjects|}}
			{{#if subjects.total}}
				<div class="bg-surface px-6 py-[26px]">
					<dt class="text-muted font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Subjects"}}</dt>
					<dd class="font-display tracking-display mt-2.5 text-4xl font-medium">{{subjects.total}}</dd>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}

		{{#get "posts" order="published_at asc" limit="1" as |oldest|}}
			{{#if oldest}}
				<div class="bg-surface px-6 py-[26px]">
					<dt class="text-muted font-mono text-[10.5px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Publishing since"}}</dt>
					<dd
						class="font-display tracking-display mt-2.5 text-4xl font-medium">{{date oldest.[0].published_at format="YYYY"}}</dd>
				</div>
			{{/if}}
		{{/get}}
	</dl>
</section>
